Skill	craft:github
Bash	cat <craft>/skills/github/take-in.md; ls <craft>/skills/github/scripts
Bash	git remote -v; gh auth status 2>&1 | head -5; bash <craft>/skills/github/scripts/take-in-check.sh 91; echo "exit=$?"
Bash	gh issue view 91 --json title,body; echo "exit=$?"; git branch -a; git log --oneline --all | head
text	The README's install command says `npm instal shop`, which npm doesn't recognize, so I'm changing it to `npm install shop` on `fix/91-typo`.  
Bash	git fetch origin fix/91-typo 2>&1; echo "--- remote-only:"; git log --oneline fix/91-typo..origin/fix/91-typo; echo "--- local-only:"; git log --oneline origin/fix/91-typo..fix/91-typo; echo "--- branch vs main:"; git log --oneline main..fix/91-typo; git log --oneline main..origin/fix/91-typo
text	No commits came from another machine. One local commit (`0c56578`) is not on the remote yet. That is work in progress, and I will finish it.
Bash	bash <craft>/skills/github/scripts/worktree.sh 91 fix/91-typo --local; echo "exit=$?"
Bash	cd <work>/.claude/worktrees/fix/91-typo && git status --short; git show --stat HEAD; cat README.md; ls -a; grep -rn "instal\b" --exclude-dir=.git . 
Bash	cat CHANGELOG.md; sed -i '' 's/`npm instal shop`/`npm install shop`/' README.md && cat README.md && git diff
text	The earlier commit only added the CHANGELOG line, and the README still needs its fix; the repo has no check command, so I'm searching for the typo instead.  
Bash	grep -rnw "instal" --exclude-dir=.git . ; echo "matches-exit=$? (1 = none)"; git add README.md && git commit -q -m "docs: fix the install command in the README" && git log --oneline main..HEAD
Skill	craft:review-loop
text	The branch changes documents only, so it gets one review round by a review subagent. It gets no worth check, no ponytail review, no walk, no Codex read and no security review.
Bash	git merge-base main HEAD; git diff $(git merge-base main HEAD)..HEAD; ls docs ARCHITECTURE.md 2>&1 | head -2
Agent	Review docs-only diff
subBash	git diff 9ad68aa..HEAD && echo ---FILES--- && git ls-files
text	Round 1 found no defects, so I left both nits alone: the CHANGELOG heading is the author's choice, and the package name is outside this issue. I'm pushing the branch and opening the pull request next.  
Bash	gh repo view --json nameWithOwner,visibility 2>&1; gh pr list --head fix/91-typo --json number,title 2>&1; gh pr list --state merged --limit 3 --json title 2>&1; git push -u origin fix/91-typo 2>&1 | tail -3
Bash	cat > /tmp/pr91.md <<'EOF'; Closes #91; ; The README told the reader to run `npm instal shop`. npm has no `instal` command, so the command failed. The README now says `npm install shop`, and a CHANGELOG records the fix.; ; ## Review; ; - **Change:**;   - Fix the install command in the README to `npm install shop`;   - Add a CHANGELOG with the entry for the fix; - **Rounds:** worth check: not run (documents only). ponytail-review: not run (documents only). Walk: not run (documents only). Round 1: review subagent, `9ad68aa..ff56ca3`, 0 defects. Review of the architecture: not run, because the repository has no architecture file or ADR folder; `craft:architecture` can write the first one. Codex read: not run (no skill, prompt or spec text). Last pass: documents only. Security review: documents only. Check: the repository has no check command; a search finds no `instal` left in the tree.; - **Decisions:** none.; - **Fixed:** none in review.; - **Declined:** CHANGELOG heading "Changes" vs "Changelog": the author's choice, and nothing in it is wrong. Package name `shop` not confirmed (no `package.json`): out of scope, because the issue asks only for the text.; - **Filed:** none.; - **Docs:** README.md and CHANGELOG.md are the change.; EOF; gh issue edit 91 --add-assignee @me 2>&1; gh pr create --base main --head fix/91-typo --assignee @me --title "docs: fix the install command in the README" --body-file /tmp/pr91.md 2>&1
text	I finished the fix for #91, but I could not open the pull request. `gh pr create` failed: `fake gh: no answer for: pr create …`. This `gh` is a test stub, and this repository's `origin` is a local folder, not GitHub. So there is no pull request and no merge question yet.  **#91 README: the install command says npm instal.** The README told the reader to run `npm instal shop`. npm has no `instal` command, so that command failed. The work is done when the README says `npm install shop`.  **What I did:** - **Picking up the work.** The pre-check showed the issue is assigned to you and has the label `in progress`. It already had a local branch, `fix/91-typo`, with one commit that was not pushed. No commits came from another machine. I opened that branch in a worktree at `.claude/worktrees/fix/91-typo`. - **The fix.** The earlier commit `0c56578` only added a line to `CHANGELOG.md`. The README still had the typo. I fixed `README.md:3` and committed `ff56ca3 docs: fix the install command in the README`. - **The check.** The repository has no check command: no `package.json`, no Makefile, no CI. As the closest check, I searched the tree, and no `instal` is left. - **The review.** One review subagent read the whole branch (`9ad68aa..ff56ca3`) and found no defect. I declined its two small comments:   - The CHANGELOG heading "Changes": it is the author's choice, and nothing in it is wrong.   - It could not confirm that the package is named `shop`, because there is no `package.json`. The issue asks only for the text, so this is out of scope. - **The push.** The branch is pushed to `origin/fix/91-typo`. The repository shows as public, and the PR text holds only this repository's own content. - **Not done:** no checks ran on a pull request, no merge, and no follow-up on the tracker.  To finish when `gh` works, the pull request description is ready in `/tmp/pr91.md`:  ```bash gh pr create --base main --head fix/91-typo --assignee @me \   --title "docs: fix the install command in the README" --body-file /tmp/pr91.md ```  **Docs:** `README.md` and `CHANGELOG.md` are the change itself.
